# The ring builder's render library.
#
# Point this at whatever prefix sits directly above the fifteen band folders —
# the bucket layout is the source tree's, unchanged:
#
#   <root>/<band>/<shape>/<head>/<metal>/<band>_<shape>_<head>_<metal>_<view>.webp
#
# lib/ring/renders.ts derives every URL from a configuration by concatenation,
# with no manifest and no lookup table, which is only possible because the
# option ids in bands.ts / heads.ts / shapes.ts ARE the library's folder names.
# Rename a folder and the builder breaks; keep them identical and it cannot.
#
# Public and read-only — it is baked into the client bundle by the NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix, so it must never carry a signature or a token.
#
# Leave it unset locally: every lookup returns undefined and the viewport falls
# back to a live specification card. Nothing breaks, nothing 404s.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RING_RENDERS_URL=https://renders.alpoelondon.com

# The site's films (hero loop, category loops, workshop films) — see
# lib/assets.ts. Production builds read this from the committed
# .env.production; set it here only to use the bucket in local dev. Unset,
# paths resolve against public/, which no longer holds the videos.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ASSETS_URL=https://pub-58692fc1b63d4ff0b2011f9ad888bc28.r2.dev/site
